This directory holds the built client, which console/embed.go embeds into the
Runtime binary through `//go:embed all:dist`.

The build output is not tracked. Build it with:

    cd console/web && npm ci && npm run build

This placeholder is tracked, and it is what keeps the embed pattern valid before
the client has ever been built: the embed directive fails to compile if the
directory matches no files. The Vite build intentionally does not empty this
directory so that the placeholder survives. Delete the generated files if you
want, but keep a file here.

A Runtime built without the client reports assets_not_built to the browser and
prints the commands above, instead of serving an empty page.